course: dictionary
lesson: 9910
title: Talons: sharp claws in nature and stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A talon is a long, sharp, curved claw on the foot of a bird of prey, such as an eagle, owl or hawk. Birds use talons to grip and hold their food. «It spots a hare far below, folds its wings and drops like a stone, then swings its talons forward at the last moment.» The talons are what catch the hare.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Sharp» and «curved» tell you what a talon looks like, and «swings» and «grip» tell you what it does. Try the swap test: if you put "claw" in the sentence and it still makes sense, talon means a special kind of claw.
explain: In stories, talons can be any sharp claws or long fingernails that look frightening. A monster or witch might have talons to sound scary. «Sharp talons» and «eagle's talons» are common phrases, so look for them in your reading.
fact: A talon is a long, sharp, curved claw on the foot of a bird of prey.
fact: In stories, «talons» can mean any sharp claws or long fingernails that look frightening.
fact: An eagle's foot has four talons: three point forward and one points back.
fact: The back talon is often the biggest, and it works like a thumb to pin prey.
fact: The harpy eagle has talons around 13 cm long.
exercise: «It spots a hare far below, folds its wings and drops like a stone, then swings its talons forward at the last moment.» What are talons in this sentence? | The eyes that spot the hare | Soft feathers on the wings | *Sharp, curved claws on a bird's foot | A kind of hooked beak
exercise: Which bird is said to have talons around 13 cm long? | The penguin | The hen | *The harpy eagle | The robin
exercise: Tennyson's poem says «He clasps the crag with crooked hands» about an eagle. Which word would be more accurate for an eagle's grip? | feathers | gloves | *talons | pencils
test: In a scary story, a witch has long, sharp talons. What might talons mean here? | Tiny shiny buttons | Wings made of paper | Soft, warm pockets | *Long, sharp fingernails or claws that look frightening
test: Why does a trainer wear a thick leather glove when working with a bird of prey? | *To protect their hand from the talons | To stop the bird from flying anywhere | To keep the bird warm in winter | To make the bird's feathers shine
exam: Ruby says talon is just another word for beak. Which answer is best? | A talon is a feather on a bird's wing | Talons are only found on fish | Ruby is right, they mean the same thing | *Ruby is wrong: a talon is a sharp claw on the foot, and a beak is the hooked part of the mouth
